module glucoamylaseDetection
module maltodextrinGrowthDetection
module fermentationDetection

manifest IDY1_Cells
manifest IDY2_Cells
manifest YPD_Media
manifest MUG_Alpha_Substrate
manifest PhosphateBuffer_pH7_5
manifest BSA_Solution
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant
manifest SpacerOil
manifest MaltodextrinMedia
manifest SyntheticBeverageMedia

// ============================================================
// A Microfluidic Multiplex Sorter for Strain Development
// Leal-Alves, Dumont, Deng, Alkhaldi, Leung, Oeser, Shih
// Adv. Mater. Technol. 2025, 10, 2401209
// DOI: 10.1002/admt.202401209
//
// Protocol: Droplet-digital multiplex electrostatic sorting
// of genome-shuffled diastatic yeast (S. cerevisiae var.
// diastaticus) based on two fluorescence thresholds of
// glucoamylase activity, followed by post-HTS strain
// recovery and beverage fermentation evaluation.
//
// BIOLOGICAL OVERVIEW:
//   Two diastatic yeast strains (IDY1 and IDY2), isolated
//   from the beverage industry, are genome-shuffled via
//   self-mating to generate libraries of >10^7 variants.
//   Single cells are encapsulated in 30 pL droplets with
//   YPD media and the fluorescent glucoamylase substrate
//   4-methylumbelliferyl-alpha-D-glucopyranoside (4-MUG-a).
//   After 48 h incubation off-chip at 30 C, droplets are
//   re-injected into the multiplex electrostatic sorter
//   (15 kHz, 105 Vrms) and partitioned into two gates:
//     GT1 (gate-SC1): high fluorescence (top 95th percentile)
//     GT2 (gate-SC2): mid fluorescence (85th percentile)
//   Non-selected waste droplets flow to the central channel.
//   Recovered colonies are screened on maltodextrin and the
//   best performers are selected for beverage fermentation.
//
// SUBSTRATE NOTE:
//   4-MUG-a (4-methylumbelliferyl-alpha-D-glucopyranoside)
//   was validated for glucoamylase detection at pH 7.5 with
//   a fluorescence readout (ex 360 nm / em 450 nm). This
//   substrate is used in preference to 4-NPM (absorbance)
//   because fluorescence detection is more sensitive and
//   compatible with droplet path lengths at 30 pL volume.
//   All droplets contain 2 mM 4-MUG-a in 0.1 M phosphate
//   buffer pH 7.5 and 10% BSA to reduce surface adsorption.
//
// DROPLET GENERATION NOTE:
//   Cells are co-encapsulated with substrate at a Poisson
//   ratio (lambda = 0.3) for single-cell occupancy:
//     30 pL -> 2x10^7 cells/mL
//   Droplets are generated at T-junction generators in
//   HFE7500 oil with 2% fluorosurfactant and collected
//   into PCR tubes for off-chip incubation.
//
// SORTER DESIGN NOTE:
//   Co-planar electrostatic electrodes (SE1 and SE2) are
//   activated at 15 kHz / 105 Vrms to laterally displace
//   droplets from the central waste channel (WC) into
//   sorting channels SC1 (high) or SC2 (mid). Sorting
//   throughput: 160 Hz for 30 pL droplets. False negative
//   rate: ~3%. No pressure rebalancing or redesign is
//   required when switching droplet sizes (30-1000 pL).
//   `mix` steps below abstract electrode-actuated droplet
//   merging and flow-through sorting events.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- entry: cell prep, genome shuffling,
//                              droplet encapsulation, off-chip
//                              incubation, sorter re-injection
//   BB2  highGatePass       -- gt1Signal > 0: high-fitness droplet
//                              sorted into SC1; recover colonies
//   BB3  highGateFail       -- gt1Signal <= 0: not high-fitness;
//                              continue to mid-gate check
//   BB4  highGateJoin       -- join: mid-gate branch begins
//   BB5  midGatePass        -- gt2Signal > 0: mid-fitness droplet
//                              sorted into SC2; recover colonies
//   BB6  midGateFail        -- gt2Signal <= 0: waste; drain
//   BB7  midGateJoin        -- join: post-HTS recovery branch
//   BB8  maltodextrinPass   -- growthSignal > 0: improved growth;
//                              select for fermentation assay
//   BB9  maltodextrinFail   -- growthSignal <= 0: no improvement;
//                              drain
//   BB10 fermentationPass   -- fermentSignal > 0: improved
//                              fermentation; dispose (strain banked)
//   BB11 fermentationFail   -- fermentSignal <= 0: no fermentation
//                              improvement; drain
//   BB12 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prepare diastatic yeast cell suspension.
//   IDY1 or IDY2 parental strains grown overnight in YPD
//   broth at 30 C / 200 rpm. Cultures sonicated and washed
//   3x with PBS by centrifugation. Final pellet resuspended
//   in 2x YPD broth (buffered at pH 7.5).
//   Cell concentration adjusted for Poisson lambda = 0.3:
//     30 pL droplets -> 2x10^7 cells/mL
//   10% (w/w) BSA added to reduce surface adsorption.
//
//   NOTE: This .bs file encodes the IDY1 arm as the
//   representative protocol. A separate file should be
//   used for IDY2 with IDY2_Cells as the manifest entry.
//   Both arms use identical sorter parameters and assay
//   conditions; only the parental strain differs.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellSuspension   = dispense 1 units of IDY1_Cells
bsaAdditive      = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
cellsWithBSA     = mix cellSuspension with bsaAdditive for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Prepare fluorescent glucoamylase substrate.
//   4-MUG-a prepared at 4 mM in 0.1 M phosphate buffer
//   pH 7.5. Co-encapsulated 1:1 with cell suspension to
//   yield a final droplet concentration of 2 mM 4-MUG-a.
//   Phosphate buffer keeps pH neutral for cell viability
//   while providing sufficient glucoamylase signal at 30 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

phosphateBuffer  = dispense 1 units of PhosphateBuffer_pH7_5
mugSubstrate     = dispense 1 units of MUG_Alpha_Substrate
assayMix         = mix mugSubstrate with phosphateBuffer for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Co-encapsulate single cells with substrate in 30 pL
//   droplets at T-junction generator.
//   Cell solution mixed 1:1 with substrate solution; droplets
//   formed in HFE7500 oil + 2% fluorosurfactant.
//   Droplet size set by T-junction geometry (40 um channel,
//   30 pL target volume, D = 40 um diameter).
//   `mix` abstracts the T-junction co-flow encapsulation
//   event; this is a pressure-driven droplet generation step,
//   not a DMF electrode mixing operation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilCarrier          = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
encapsulatedDroplets = mix cellsWithBSA with assayMix for 5s
dropletsInOil        = mix encapsulatedDroplets with oilCarrier for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Off-chip incubation for 48 h at 30 C.
//   Droplets collected into PCR tubes with 50 uL of 2%
//   fluorosurfactant in HFE7500 and incubated in the dark
//   at 30 C. Fluorescence and bright-field images taken
//   every 24 h to monitor cell growth and glucoamylase
//   activity. 48 h selected based on optimisation data
//   showing peak fluorescence at this timepoint for 30 pL
//   droplets (IDY1: ~3 a.u.; IDY2: ~1 a.u.).
//   48 h = 2880 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat dropletsInOil at 30c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Re-inject incubated droplets into multiplex sorter.
//   Droplets re-injected through 1/32" OD PEEK tubing at:
//     Re-injection flow rate: 3 nL/s
//     Spacer oil flow rate: 300 nL/s
//   Fluorescence population measured and displayed as a
//   histogram (Gaussian distribution, n ~= 720,000 droplets
//   screened at 160 Hz) to set sorting gate thresholds:
//     gate-SC1 (GT1): high fluorescence, 95th percentile
//     gate-SC2 (GT2): mid fluorescence, 85th percentile
//   `mix` abstracts the re-injection and flow-through
//   fluorescence interrogation event at the sorter inlet.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spacerOil           = dispense 1 units of SpacerOil
reinjectedDroplets  = mix dropletsInOil with spacerOil for 1s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Fluorescence detection for multiplex gate assignment.
//   glucoamylaseDetection module abstracts in-line optical
//   fiber fluorescence measurement (ex 470 nm LED, emission
//   collected at 450 nm via bandpass filter). Signal measured
//   by in-house automation software and used to determine
//   which sorting electrode (SE1 or SE2) to actuate.
//   Detection window: 0.4 ms travel time at 160 Hz.
//   GT1 signal > 0: high fluorescence (SC1 sort)
//   GT2 signal > 0: mid fluorescence (SC2 sort)
//   Waste: neither threshold exceeded (central WC channel)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gt1Signal = detect glucoamylaseDetection on reinjectedDroplets for 1s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: High-fitness gate (GT1 / SC1)
// Pass (BB2): gt1Signal > 0 -> high-glucoamylase droplet
//   detected above 95th percentile; actuate SE1 (15 kHz,
//   105 Vrms) to deflect into SC1. Recover into pipette tip.
// Fail (BB3): gt1Signal <= 0 -> not high-fitness; do not
//   actuate SE1; proceed to mid-gate evaluation (BB4).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (highGateJoin).
// ============================================================

if (gt1Signal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // HIGH-FITNESS RECOVERY (GT1 / SC1):
    //   Droplet deflected to SC1 by SE1 electrode actuation.
    //   Sorted droplets collected by pipetting the top layer
    //   of the oil emulsion from pipette tips at the SC1
    //   outlet. Aliquots (5 uL) diluted into 50 uL YPD broth,
    //   plated on YPD agar plates, and incubated at 30 C for
    //   48 h. Several colonies selected for post-HTS analysis.
    //   High-sorted IDY1 strains labelled H2, H3 (paper).
    //   High-sorted IDY2 strains labelled H13, H23 (paper).
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    highFitnessDroplet = mix reinjectedDroplets with spacerOil for 1s
    dispose highFitnessDroplet
} else {
    drain reinjectedDroplets
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: highGateJoin
// Dispose GT1 QC signal. Control falls into mid-gate
// evaluation branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose gt1Signal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Mid-fitness gate evaluation (GT2 / SC2).
//   For droplets that did not exceed the GT1 threshold,
//   the automation software evaluates whether the signal
//   exceeds the GT2 (mid, 85th percentile) threshold.
//   If yes, SE2 is actuated (15 kHz, 105 Vrms) to deflect
//   the droplet into SC2. If no, the droplet flows to the
//   central waste channel (WC) undeflected.
//   `detect` here abstracts the second threshold evaluation
//   performed on the same re-injected droplet population
//   (the sorter evaluates GT1 then GT2 sequentially per drop).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gt2Signal = detect glucoamylaseDetection on spacerOil for 1s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Mid-fitness gate (GT2 / SC2)
// Pass (BB5): gt2Signal > 0 -> mid-glucoamylase droplet
//   detected above 85th percentile; actuate SE2 (15 kHz,
//   105 Vrms) to deflect into SC2. Recover into pipette tip.
// Fail (BB6): gt2Signal <= 0 -> below both thresholds;
//   droplet flows undeflected into WC (waste). Drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (midGateJoin).
// ============================================================

if (gt2Signal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // MID-FITNESS RECOVERY (GT2 / SC2):
    //   Droplet deflected to SC2 by SE2 electrode actuation.
    //   Recovery, plating, and incubation identical to GT1.
    //   Mid-sorted IDY1 strains labelled M2, M23 (paper).
    //   Mid-sorted IDY2 strains labelled M9, M22 (paper).
    //   KEY FINDING: Mid-selected strains (IDY1-M23, IDY2-M9)
    //   showed superior fermentation performance vs high-selected
    //   strains, attributed to lower metabolic burden from
    //   balanced glucoamylase expression.
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    midFitnessDroplet = mix spacerOil with spacerOil for 1s
    dispose midFitnessDroplet
} else {
    drain spacerOil
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: midGateJoin
// Dispose GT2 QC signal. Control falls into post-HTS
// maltodextrin growth screening branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose gt2Signal

// ============================================================
// POST-HTS STEP 1: Maltodextrin growth screening (Step 3
// of paper's 4-step workflow).
// Recovered colonies (both GT1 and GT2 populations, 24
// colonies each) grown for 48 h at 30 C / 300 rpm in
// maltodextrin media (2 g/L yeast extract, 4 g/L bacto
// peptone, 20 g/L maltodextrin). Optical density at 600 nm
// measured at 24 h and 48 h. Growth fold improvement
// calculated relative to wild-type parental strain.
// Maltodextrin growth evaluates starch-utilisation capacity,
// an industrially relevant parameter for beverage fermentation.
//
// NOTE: In the paper, all 24 colonies per gate are screened
// simultaneously in parallel wells. The BioScript abstraction
// below models a single representative colony going through
// sequential evaluation steps (growth -> fermentation).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Inoculate recovered colony into maltodextrin media.
//   5 uL from sorted population plated; overnight glycerol
//   stocks prepared; then 5 uL inoculated into 1 mL
//   maltodextrin media for growth measurement.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

maltodextrinMedia   = dispense 1 units of MaltodextrinMedia
ypd_preculture      = dispense 1 units of YPD_Media
recoveredColony     = mix maltodextrinMedia with ypd_preculture for 5s

// Incubation at 30 C for 48 h (= 2880 min).
// OD600 measured at 24 h and 48 h via plate reader.
heat recoveredColony at 30c for 2880m

// Maltodextrin growth QC signal: OD600 at 48 h vs wild type.
growthSignal = detect maltodextrinGrowthDetection on recoveredColony for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Maltodextrin growth QC gate
// Pass (BB8): growthSignal > 0 -> improved growth vs WT;
//   strain carries forward to fermentation assay.
// Fail (BB9): growthSignal <= 0 -> no growth improvement;
//   drain (strain not selected for fermentation).
// Both branches converge at BB10/BB11 (fermentation branch).
// ============================================================

if (growthSignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // IMPROVED GROWTH:
    //   Strain exhibits statistically significant growth
    //   improvement in maltodextrin vs wild type.
    //   IDY2 GT1 and GT2 strains showed on average 2.2x and
    //   1.7x more growth respectively (paper Figure 5C).
    //   IDY1-H2 and IDY1-M2 showed ~2.5x and ~1.4x improvement
    //   respectively (paper Figure 5A).
    //   Strain selected for fermentation evaluation (STEP 3->4).
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    dispose recoveredColony
} else {
    drain recoveredColony
}

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: Fermentation evaluation in synthetic beverage
// media (Step 4 of paper's 4-step workflow).
// Selected mutant strains evaluated in lab-scale fermentation
// assay mimicking industrial beverage conditions.
// Media (3 mL synthetic medium per vial):
//   125 g/L maltose, 60 g/L maltodextrin, 1 mL ethanol,
//   1.25 mL 50% glycerol, 3 mL 85% lactic acid,
//   2 g/L yeast extract, 6.4 g/L bactopeptone,
//   pH 5.9, 25 mg/mL chloramphenicol.
// Inoculation: 100 uL preculture into 3 mL synthetic media.
// Temperature: 20 C for 22 h, then 30 C until 72 h endpoint.
// Monitoring: CO2 release by weight loss at 0, 18, 24, 42,
//   48, 66, 72 h. Fermentation complete at 72 h (final mass
//   loss point). Dry biomass weight by pelleting at 60 C.
// Metric: CO2 released per mg biomass; ethanol yield normalised
//   to dry biomass.
//
// KEY RESULT: Mid-level sorted strains (IDY1-M23, IDY2-M9)
//   outperformed high-level sorted strains in fermentation
//   efficiency, producing more CO2 per mg biomass and higher
//   ethanol yields. IDY1-M23 showed the highest CO2 mass loss
//   (~7.8 mg CO2/mg biomass vs ~5.01 for WT at 72 h).
//   IDY2-M9 and IDY2-H13 showed improved CO2 mass loss rates
//   (~0.128 and ~0.105 h^-1 respectively vs WT).
//
// NOTE ON TEMPERATURE SEQUENCE:
//   The fermentation protocol uses a two-phase temperature
//   profile: 20 C for 22 h then 30 C for the remaining 50 h.
//   BioScript `heat` statements are used sequentially to
//   model this ramp; the compiler treats them as serial
//   heating events on the same fluid variable.
//   22 h = 1320 min; 50 h = 3000 min; total = 72 h.
// ============================================================

syntheticMedia      = dispense 1 units of SyntheticBeverageMedia
ypd_ferment_pre     = dispense 1 units of YPD_Media

// Preculture: 48 h at 30 C / 300 rpm in YPD before inoculation.
// 48 h = 2880 min.
heat ypd_ferment_pre at 30c for 2880m

// Inoculate 100 uL preculture into synthetic beverage media.
fermentationMix     = mix syntheticMedia with ypd_ferment_pre for 5m

// Phase 1: 20 C for 22 h (= 1320 min). Initial fermentation phase.
heat fermentationMix at 20c for 1320m

// Phase 2: 30 C for 50 h (= 3000 min). Main fermentation phase.
heat fermentationMix at 30c for 3000m

// Detect fermentation performance: CO2 release, ethanol yield.
// fermentationDetection abstracts CO2 weight-loss measurement
// and end-point ethanol determination from dried biomass.
fermentSignal = detect fermentationDetection on fermentationMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: Fermentation performance QC gate
// Pass (BB10): fermentSignal > 0 -> improved CO2 release
//   and/or ethanol yield vs WT parental strain; strain
//   banked as a superior industrial candidate.
// Fail (BB11): fermentSignal <= 0 -> no fermentation
//   improvement; drain (strain not selected).
// Both branches converge at BB12 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (fermentSignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // FERMENTATION IMPROVEMENT CONFIRMED:
    //   Strain shows statistically significant improvement in
    //   CO2 release and/or ethanol yield relative to WT.
    //   Top producers: IDY1-M23 (mid-gate), IDY2-M9 (mid-gate).
    //   Both would have been missed by a binary (GT1-only)
    //   screening approach, validating the multiplex strategy.
    //   Hypothesised mechanism: balanced glucoamylase expression
    //   in mid-level strains avoids metabolic burden from
    //   high-level enzyme overproduction, maintaining resources
    //   for growth and fermentation.
    //   Strain disposed (banked for industrial use).
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    dispose fermentationMix
} else {
    drain fermentationMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB12: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Dispose growth and fermentation signals.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose growthSignal
dispose fermentSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
